{"tool_name":"bayestyper","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"bayestyper","version":"1.5","home":"https://github.com/bioinformatics-centre/BayesTyper","documentation":"https://github.com/bioinformatics-centre/BayesTyper/blob/v1.5/README.md","license":"MIT","summary":"A method for variant graph genotyping based on exact alignment of k-mers.","identifiers":["biotools:bayestyper","doi:10.1038/s41588-018-0145-5"],"build":{"number":4,"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"build":["make",null,"cmake"],"host":["zlib","boost-cpp"],"run":["boost-cpp"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/bioinformatics-centre/BayesTyper/archive/v1.5.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["bayesTyper | grep \"BayesTyper\"","bayesTyperTools | grep \"BayesTyperTools\""]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"bayestyper","identifiers":["biotools:bayestyper","doi:10.1038/s41588-018-0145-5"],"license":"MIT","summary":"A method for variant graph genotyping based on exact alignment of k-mers","home_url":"https://github.com/bioinformatics-centre/BayesTyper","keywords":["Genetic Variation","Genome, Human","Genotype","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Sequence Analysis, DNA","Sequence assembly","Whole genome sequencing","DNA polymorphism","Genetics"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"bayestyper","home":"https://github.com/bioinformatics-centre/BayesTyper","summary":"Perform genotyping of all types of variation (including SNPs, indels and complex structural variants) based on an input set of variants and read k-mer counts.","addition_date":"2018-07-07T20:53:37Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:27:14.050034Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bayestyper","credit":[{"email":"jasi@binf.ku.dk","name":"Jonas Andreas Sibbesen","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"lasse.maretty@clin.au.dk","name":"Lasse Maretty","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/bioinformatics-centre/BayesTyper#why-should-i-use-bayestyper"},{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://github.com/bioinformatics-centre/BayesTyper#usage"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Polymorphism detection","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3202"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"BayesTyper","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"migle_sur","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41588-018-0145-5","metadata":{"abstract":"Genotype estimates from short-read sequencing data are typically based on the alignment of reads to a linear reference, but reads originating from more complex variants (for example, structural variants) often align poorly, resulting in biased genotype estimates. This bias can be mitigated by first collecting a set of candidate variants across discovery methods, individuals and databases, and then realigning the reads to the variants and reference simultaneously. However, this realignment problem has proved computationally difficult. Here, we present a new method (BayesTyper) that uses exact alignment of read k-mers to a graph representation of the reference and variants to efficiently perform unbiased, probabilistic genotyping across the variation spectrum. We demonstrate that BayesTyper generally provides superior variant sensitivity and genotyping accuracy relative to existing methods when used to integrate variants across discovery approaches and individuals. Finally, we demonstrate that including a 'variation-prior' database containing already known variants significantly improves sensitivity.","authors":[{"name":"Krogh A."},{"name":"Maretty L."},{"name":"Sibbesen J.A."}],"citationCount":45,"date":"2018-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Genetics","title":"Accurate genotyping across variant classes and lengths using variant graphs"},"pmid":"29915429","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":